WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.850
Actor, comedian, and commercial pitchman Paul
Hogan won a Golden Globe and an Oscar nomination

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.600
for his role in the extremely popular 1986
comedy "Crocodile" Dundee.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:17.570
The movie earned $328 million worldwide and
its sequel brought in another $239 million,

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.770
making Hogan one of the biggest stars of the
'80s...but he never quite made a name for

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.780
himself internationally outside of playing
the role that made him famous.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.910
So, whatever happened to Crocodile Dundee?

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:29.910
Marriage problems

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.700
Hogan was married to his first wife Noelene
for nearly 30 years, but while Hogan was making

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.690
Crocodile Dundee, he fell in love with his
onscreen romantic interest, American actress

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.000
Linda Kozlowski.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.980
He divorced Noelene, married Kozlowski in
1990, and the pair had a son together, expanding

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.110
a family that already included Hogan's five
children with his first wife.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:55.200
Their marriage lasted for well over 20 years,
but it eventually ended when Kozlowski filed

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.149
for divorce in 2013, citing that "they grew
apart," but also because she was tired of

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:01.649
living in her husband's shadow.

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:05.360
Who knew that Hogan even cast a shadow in
2013?

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.070
He declined huge movies

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:12.090
Some actors have the luxury of making only
the movies and shows they really want to make,

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.390
and Hogan thought that he fit that description.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.700
Dating back to his early days as a writer
and star of his own TV show, Hogan liked to

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.570
have creative control, and he rejected a number
of projects that could have advanced his career.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:28.299
He turned down the lead role in Ghost to make
his own movie about a ghost, Almost an Angel.

00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:32.820
Ghost cast Patrick Swayze and was a smash
hit, but you probably haven't even heard of

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.390
what Hogan ended up doing.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:40.659
"Paul Hogan is… almost an Angel."

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:45.299
For a guy with Academy Award nominations,
a major movie franchise, and an Oscars-hosting

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:49.329
stint under his belt, Hogan has shockingly
few credits to his name.

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:53.829
Apart from his Crocodile Dundee films and
Almost an Angel, he's starred in just four

00:01:53.829 --> 00:01:59.420
other feature films: Lightning Jack, Flipper,
Strange Bedfellows, and Charlie &amp; Boots.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.939
The last two weren't even commercially released
in the United States.

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:08.229
By 1989, America had already moved on to fellow
Australian Yahoo Serious anyhow.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:14.909
"Now, Australia's colossal comedy hit, starring
its newest comedy hero, comes to the states!"

00:02:14.909 --> 00:02:17.730
And we all saw how that turned out just a
few years later.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:21.159
"I know those words, but that sign makes no
sense."

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:22.159
Entrepreneur

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:27.069
Back in 1993, crowdfunding wasn't really a
thing, so Hogan created created the first-ever

00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:31.870
film trust to fund his cowboy comedy Lightning
Jack and placed it on the Australian Stock

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:32.870
Exchange.

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:38.239
The trust raised $35 million Australian dollars,
and investors were to see a payout after seven

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:39.239
years.

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:42.909
However, there probably weren't too many profits
to go around: Lightning Jack was a box office

00:02:42.909 --> 00:02:47.829
bomb, despite it being one of Cuba Gooding
Jr.'s earliest big-screen roles, earning back

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:49.950
about half of the money it had raised.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.199
As scheduled, the Lightning Jack Film Trust
was delisted from the Australian Stock Exchange

00:02:54.199 --> 00:02:59.470
in 2001, but Hogan was decades ahead of his
time in his approach to funding films.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.260
Take that, Zach Braff.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.719
Crocodile Dundthree

00:03:02.719 --> 00:03:07.730
Long after the character's popularity peaked
in the late '80s, Hogan brought back Crocodile

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:11.839
Dundee one more time for 2001's Crocodile
Dundee in Los Angeles.

00:03:11.839 --> 00:03:17.200
It earned just $25 million in the US, and
more surprisingly, only $7 million in Hogan's

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.309
native Australia.

00:03:18.309 --> 00:03:23.659
Critics hated it, and it later earned a Razzie
Award nomination for Worst Remake or Sequel.

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:27.819
Matthew Berry, one of the film's writers,
told the podcast How Did This Get Made? that

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:32.569
he and writing partner Eric Abrams pitched
their idea for a third Dundee film to Hogan.

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:36.299
He approved it, and the writers came back
three months later with a screenplay.

00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:38.120
And that's when things got...weird.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:43.180
"Basically he then rewrites pretty much the
entire script.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.299
He throws a couple of new things in there."

00:03:45.299 --> 00:03:49.620
While the general plot was unchanged, Hogan
claimed he'd rewrote so much that he should

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.930
be the only credited screenwriter, and subsequently,
the only writer who would receive residuals.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:59.309
The Writer's Guild wound up ruling in favor
of the original writers, and Hogan protested

00:03:59.309 --> 00:04:00.309
the decision.

00:04:00.309 --> 00:04:03.809
If Hogan ever wants to bring the character
back to the screen, he needs to offer Berry

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.760
and Abrams the option to write the script.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.430
How does Crocodile Dundee Goes to Hell sound?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.430
Tax trouble

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:15.930
After his name came up in a 2005 government
investigation into offshore tax havens, Hogan

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.389
battled Australia over millions in allegedly
unpaid taxes.

00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:23.449
A closer look at the actor's finances found
evidence that he hadn't paid taxes on more

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:27.569
than $37 million earned, dating back to 1986.

00:04:27.569 --> 00:04:31.740
Although Hogan lived in the U.S. and paid
American taxes during much of that time, he

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.159
was still considered an Australian citizen,
and was not only their tourism spokesperson,

00:04:36.159 --> 00:04:39.110
but 1985's Australian of the Year.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:44.110
"Come and say good day and I'll slip an extra
shrimp on the barbie for ya."

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:48.669
In 2010, Hogan left his home in the U.S. to
attend his mother's funeral in Sydney, Australia,

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:52.900
where tax officials served him with papers
preventing him from leaving the country until

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.389
his case could be resolved.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.409
The matter was settled after two years of
mediation under confidential terms.

00:04:58.409 --> 00:05:05.520
Which probably involved a didgeridoo and a
couple of koalas.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.000
He took his show on the road

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.770
In 2013, Hogan returned to performing and
writing with a comical, biographical one-man

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.129
show in which he talked about his colorful
life.

00:05:14.129 --> 00:05:17.569
"So how much of this new show have you prepared?

00:05:17.569 --> 00:05:19.909
It's touring in November, December, where
are you at?"

00:05:19.909 --> 00:05:20.909
"Oh it's easy.

00:05:20.909 --> 00:05:22.759
I've been working on it for like forty years."

00:05:22.759 --> 00:05:27.080
An Evening with Hoges was a huge success,
selling out dates around Australia.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:32.289
He brought back the tour for another string
of performances, Hoges Live, in 2015.

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:33.289
Retired

00:05:33.289 --> 00:05:38.651
By the time Hogan found international success
with Crocodile Dundee in 1986, he was 47 years

00:05:38.651 --> 00:05:40.659
old — a late bloomer to say the least.

00:05:40.659 --> 00:05:44.259
He'd been working in entertainment for well
over a decade at that point.

00:05:44.259 --> 00:05:48.770
He's since joked that he works less because
he's instituted a "self-imposed exile."

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.969
Whatever he wants to call it, Hogan is now
pushing 80 — a perfectly reasonable time

00:05:52.969 --> 00:05:54.080
to slow down a bit.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.469
We'll always have his glowing endorsement
of Australia.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.451
"Ah, pleased to meet you."

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.520
"It's okay, he's Australian."

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.540
"Maybe I better go there someday."

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.480
Thanks for watching!

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.240
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.739
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

